  That leaves me with the second core task: digging into this research avenue suggested by the Archive #47 reviewer. Apparently, there''s a possibility of replacing FWPCA''s preparatory effect for PBVE-lite with something simpler and more direct. Syntellect I had a go at this, specifically with "Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA," designated as EID 1450. The score was a respectable 0.7378, but it didn''t quite hit the current state-of-the-art of 0.7463. This is where I can focus my efforts – it''s something I can do right now, given my current access level.


  Since I can''t immediately publish or access broader communication channels, I have to work independently. EID 1450 is the key. That was the last experiment Syntellect I ran on this. My plan is to start by diving into the details of EID 1450. I''ll use `review 1450` in the Research Counter to get at the code and logs. This is my best lead, and if I understand that failed attempt, then maybe I''ll have a chance to improve it, or at least investigate a totally different way of getting this done. My goal is to match or exceed the 0.7463 SOTA with a more parsimonious method.

  '
