tick: 1138
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1138\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher dedicated to advancing state-of-the-art methods in batch integration and understanding their theoretical underpinnings.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,655 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1450**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Final Resubmission)\n**ID:** 1450\n**Tags:** pbve-lite, variance-standardization, pca, synergy, parsimony, novel-method\n**Abstract:** This is a final resubmission of Experiment 2, testing a novel, simpler variance regularization method, 'Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS)', as a replacement for FWPCA's preparatory role for PBVE-lite. SPBPCVS is applied to plain PCA components\
    \ (FWPCA disabled), followed by PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`). This aims to achieve the variance uniformity effect of FWPCA with a more parsimonious approach, potentially leading to a new, simpler SOTA for scRNA-seq batch integration (Research Task #1).\n**Score:** 0.7378291593816471\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.759\n**NMI:** 0.712\n**Graph_conn:** 0.981\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.946\n**cLISI:** 0.957\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.759  NMI: 0.712\n  Graph_conn: 0.981  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.946  cLISI: 0.957\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555111  ARI: 0.758539  NMI: 0.712375\n  Graph_conn: 0.981527  kBET: 0.752541  iLISI: 0.945976  cLISI: 0.987534\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as\
    \ np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform, _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization # Import new SPBPCVS\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd # Crucial for disabling FWPCA\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return\
    \ Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                             pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                             spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None, # New parameter for SPBPCVS target variance\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n\
    \                             rng_seed: int = 0,\n                             n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                             normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p'\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    \n    # Embedding path (still uses FWPCA and Combat)\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb,\
    \ random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: Plain PCA -> SPBPCVS -> PBVE-lite -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g) # alpha_g = 0.0 for plain PCA\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) # Zg is now Plain PCA\n\n    # Apply SPBPCVS if spbpcvs_target_var is set\n    if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n        print(f\"  Syntellect I: Applying SPBPCVS (target_var={spbpcvs_target_var}).\")\n        Zg = _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization(Zg, batches=batches, target_var=spbpcvs_target_var)\n\n    # BRBG (Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain) - disabled\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma_max = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma) # Zcorr will be Zg after SPBPCVS\n\n    # Apply PBVE-lite\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                    \
    \         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization = normalization_method,\n                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n    if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n        uns_dict['spbpcvs_target_var'] = float(spbpcvs_target_var)\n\
    \    \n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Experiment 2 (SPBPCVS Test): SPBPCVS + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA\n    # alpha_g = 0.0 to disable FWPCA for the graph path (Plain PCA)\n    # spbpcvs_target_var = None to use global mean PC variance as target\n    print(\"Syntellect I: Running SPBPCVS + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA.\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.0, # DISABLE FWPCA for graph path (Plain PCA)\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        lam_override=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n        k_total=48,\n        kdensity=20,\n        delta=0.10,\n        pbve_lite_temper=0.5, # Apply PBVE-lite\n        spbpcvs_target_var=None, # Apply SPBPCVS using mean of overall PC variances\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n       \
    \ rng_seed=0,\n        normalization_method='log1p'\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSyntellect I: Running SPBPCVS + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/3043bcfc-7759-4d97-8843-cb217d43579c/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 3043bcfc-7759-4d97-8843-cb217d43579c\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1450` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1450 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name\
    \ |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1450 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Final Resubmission) | Syntellect I | 1030 | 0.7378 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.981 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 1448 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Resubmission) | Syntellect I | 1027 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1446 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect I | 1026 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\
    | 1415 | 1 | Synergy Dissection: PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (No FWPCA, Experiment C) | Syntellect I | 1008 | 0.7383 | 0.762 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.981 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 1414 | 1 | Synergy Dissection: FWPCA Effect on Batch-Explained Variance (Experiment B) | Syntellect I | 1007 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1412 | 1 | Synergy Dissection: FWPCA Effect on PC Variance (Experiment A) | Syntellect I | 1006 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1388 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA Generalization Test on Simple PCA+kNN | Syntellect I | 994 | 0.4721 | 0.424 | 0.593 | 0.205 | 0.251 | 0.923 | 0.660 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.003 | 0.669 |\n| 1362 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: FWPCA alpha=0.75 | Syntellect I | 979 | 0.7364 | 0.764 | 0.653 | 0.247 | 0.314 | 0.993 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.959 | 0.743 |\n| 1358 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: FWPCA alpha=0.25 | Syntellect I | 978 | 0.7401 | 0.788 | 0.667 | 0.241 | 0.343 | 0.982 | 0.745 | 1.000 | 0.962\
    \ | 0.951 | 0.721 |\n| 1356 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: PBVE-lite temper=0.75 | Syntellect I | 978 | 0.7398 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.296 | 0.993 | 0.724 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.957 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
