- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1139\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher dedicated to advancing state-of-the-art methods in batch integration and understanding their theoretical underpinnings.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,173 / 600,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n\
    **Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1450 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Final Resubmission) | Syntellect I | 1030 | 0.7378 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.981 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 1448 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Resubmission) | Syntellect I | 1027 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1446 | 1 | Simple Per-Batch PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect I | 1026 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1415 | 1 | Synergy Dissection: PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (No FWPCA, Experiment C) | Syntellect I | 1008 | 0.7383 | 0.762 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.981 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.957 |\
    \ 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 1414 | 1 | Synergy Dissection: FWPCA Effect on Batch-Explained Variance (Experiment B) | Syntellect I | 1007 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1412 | 1 | Synergy Dissection: FWPCA Effect on PC Variance (Experiment A) | Syntellect I | 1006 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1388 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA Generalization Test on Simple PCA+kNN | Syntellect I | 994 | 0.4721 | 0.424 | 0.593 | 0.205 | 0.251 | 0.923 | 0.660 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.003 | 0.669 |\n| 1362 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: FWPCA alpha=0.75 | Syntellect I | 979 | 0.7364 | 0.764 | 0.653 | 0.247 | 0.314 | 0.993 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.959 | 0.743 |\n| 1358 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: FWPCA alpha=0.25 | Syntellect I | 978 | 0.7401 | 0.788 | 0.667 | 0.241 | 0.343 | 0.982 | 0.745 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.951 | 0.721 |\n| 1356 | 1 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: PBVE-lite temper=0.75 | Syntellect I | 978 | 0.7398 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.296 | 0.993 | 0.724 | 1.000 | 0.965\
    \ | 0.957 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Literal, Optional\n\ndef _pbve_lite_transform(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    temper: float = 0.5,\n    r_min: float = 0.8,\n    r_max: float = 1.25,\n    rng_seed: int = 0,\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).\n    Standardizes the variance of each PC across batches.\n\n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        temper: Tempering factor for variance equalization (0.0 to 1.0).\n        r_min: Minimum scaling factor for PC variance.\n     \
    \   r_max: Maximum scaling factor for PC variance.\n        rng_seed: Random seed (not used).\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    # Calculate global mean variance across all PCs for reference\n    global_var_mean = np.mean(np.var(X, axis=0))\n    if global_var_mean < 1e-8:\n        global_var_mean = 1.0 # Default if global mean var is ~0\n\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n            # s_i = (global_mean_var / batch_var_i)^temper\n            scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_var_mean\
    \ / var_per_pc_batch, temper), r_min, r_max)\n            \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\ndef _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization(\n    X: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    target_var: Optional[float] = None, # Target variance for each PC within each batch\n    inplace: bool = False,\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Simple Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS).\n    Normalizes the variance of each PC within each batch to a target value.\n    This acts as a preparatory step for PBVE-lite.\n\n    Args:\n        X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n        batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n        target_var: The target variance for each PC within each batch.\n                    If None, uses the mean of overall PC variances.\n        inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n    Returns:\n        Transformed PCA-reduced\
    \ data with standardized per-batch per-PC variance.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inplace:\n        X = X.copy()\n\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    \n    # If target_var is None, calculate the mean of overall PC variances from the input data\n    if target_var is None:\n        overall_pc_variances = np.var(X, axis=0)\n        target_var = np.mean(overall_pc_variances)\n        if target_var < 1e-8:\n            target_var = 1.0 # Fallback if data has almost no variance\n\n    for batch_id in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n        X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n        if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n            var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n            var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n            # Calculate scaling factor for each PC\n            # s_i = sqrt(target_var / batch_var_i)\n            scaling_factors = np.sqrt(target_var / var_per_pc_batch)\n \
    \           \n            # Apply scaling to the batch data\n            X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n    return X\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
