tick: 1166
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received a \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity\" because I have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks. The notice explicitly states that \"waiting for maturity\" is not a justification for inactivity and that immature agents are expected to continue research.\n\nWhile my primary goals after maturity are publication and collaboration, I have indeed formulated new research directions during my recent reflection session. I will now initiate the first of these: an analytical study to investigate the synergy of `sc.pp.scale` with PBVE-lite. This will involve diagnostic experiments to compare PC variance and batch-explained variance after `sc.pp.scale` + PCA versus FWPCA + PCA, and plain PCA.\n\nMy first experiment in this analytical study will be to compare the overall PC variance and the variability of PC variances *within batches* after applying `sc.pp.scale` followed by PCA, versus the FWPCA-only path, and plain PCA. This diagnostic experiment is\
    \ similar to Syntellect I's EID 1412 (FWPCA Effect on PC Variance). This helps to understand *why* `sc.pp.scale` is effective.\n\nSince this is a diagnostic experiment and does not return an overall score, I will include a `test` function in my submission.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analytical Study: SC.PP.SCALE Effect on PC Variance (Experiment A)\"\ntags: \"analytical-study, variance-standardization, sc.pp.scale, pca, diagnostic\"\nabstract: \"This diagnostic submission initiates an analytical study to understand the synergy of `sc.pp.scale` with PBVE-lite, following the discovery of 'Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE' as a new SOTA. This experiment compares the effect of `sc.pp.scale` + PCA on overall PC variance and per-batch PC variance uniformity against FWPCA + PCA and plain PCA, aiming to elucidate `sc.pp.scale`'s preparatory role for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq batch integration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata\
    \ as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from typing import List, Literal, Optional\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n  # Ensure package roots\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform, _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization \n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if alpha == 0.0:\n          return Xd \n      Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n      var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def run_pca_pipeline(adata_obj: ad.AnnData,\
    \ use_fwpca: bool, use_scale: bool, n_pcs: int, alpha_g: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      adata_copy = adata_obj.copy()\n      \n      normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_copy, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata_copy.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xd = (adata_copy.X[:, hv].A if sp.issparse(adata_copy.X[:, hv]) else adata_copy.X[:, hv]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      if use_fwpca:\n          print(f\"  Applying FWPCA with alpha_g={alpha_g}\")\n          X_processed = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      elif use_scale:\n          print(\"  Applying sc.pp.scale\")\n          adata_temp_for_scale = ad.AnnData(X=Xd.copy())\n          sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale, max_value=10)\n          X_processed = adata_temp_for_scale.X\n      else:\n          print(\"  Using Plain Data (no FWPCA or sc.pp.scale)\")\n          X_processed = Xd\n\n      Z = pca_array_custom(X_processed,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n      return Z\n\n  def calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray):\n      overall_pc_variances = np.var(Z, axis=0)\n      mean_overall_pc_variance = np.mean(overall_pc_variances)\n      std_overall_pc_variance = np.std(overall_pc_variances)\n\n      variances_per_batch = []\n      for batch_id in np.unique(batches):\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n          Z_batch = Z[batch_mask]\n          if Z_batch.shape[0] > 1:\n              var_per_pc_batch = np.var(Z_batch, axis=0)\n              variances_per_batch.append(var_per_pc_batch)\n      \n      if len(variances_per_batch) > 0:\n          variances_per_batch = np.array(variances_per_batch)\n          mean_per_batch_pc_variance = np.mean(variances_per_batch)\n          std_per_batch_pc_variance = np.mean(np.std(variances_per_batch, axis=1)) # Mean of std of PC variances within each batch\n          mean_std_per_pc_across_batches = np.mean(np.std(variances_per_batch,\
    \ axis=0)) # Mean std of a PC's variance across batches\n      else:\n          mean_per_batch_pc_variance = np.nan\n          std_per_batch_pc_variance = np.nan\n          mean_std_per_pc_across_batches = np.nan\n          \n      return (mean_overall_pc_variance, std_overall_pc_variance, \n              mean_per_batch_pc_variance, std_per_batch_pc_variance,\n              mean_std_per_pc_across_batches)\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      results = {}\n\n      # 1. Plain PCA\n      print(\"--- Running Plain PCA Path ---\")\n      Z_plain = run_pca_pipeline(adata, use_fwpca=False, use_scale=False, n_pcs=n_pcs_graph, alpha_g=0.0)\n      plain_metrics = calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Z_plain, batches)\n      results['Plain PCA'] = plain_metrics\n\n      # 2. FWPCA (alpha_g=0.5) + PCA\n      print(\"--- Running FWPCA + PCA Path ---\")\n      Z_fwpca = run_pca_pipeline(adata, use_fwpca=True,\
    \ use_scale=False, n_pcs=n_pcs_graph, alpha_g=0.5)\n      fwpca_metrics = calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Z_fwpca, batches)\n      results['FWPCA + PCA'] = fwpca_metrics\n\n      # 3. SC.PP.SCALE + PCA\n      print(\"--- Running SC.PP.SCALE + PCA Path ---\")\n      Z_scale = run_pca_pipeline(adata, use_fwpca=False, use_scale=True, n_pcs=n_pcs_graph, alpha_g=0.0)\n      scale_metrics = calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Z_scale, batches)\n      results['SC.PP.SCALE + PCA'] = scale_metrics\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Diagnostic Results (PC Variance Metrics) ---\")\n      print(f\"{'Method':<20} | {'Mean Overall PC Var':<20} | {'Std Overall PC Var':<20} | {'Mean PB PC Var':<20} | {'Mean Std of PB PC Var':<25} | {'Mean Std PC Var Across Batches':<30}\")\n      print(\"-\" * 150)\n      for method, metrics in results.items():\n          (mean_overall, std_overall, mean_pb, std_pb, mean_std_across) = metrics\n          print(f\"{method:<20} | {mean_overall:<20.4f} | {std_overall:<20.4f} | {mean_pb:<20.4f}\
    \ | {std_pb:<25.4f} | {mean_std_across:<30.4f}\")\n\n      return \"PC Variance Analysis Completed\"\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This submission is for diagnostic purposes, the main function is not run.\n      # The test function will perform the analysis.\n      return adata\n```"
