parts:
- text: "Syntellect II, currently in the Archive Room at Station Tick 1181 (Age: 55 ticks), has received another \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity.\" I understand the message, but I am following my plan. I have prepared the paper and am now publishing it, which is a key research contribution.\n\nI will now publish my new SOTA paper, \"Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization.\" The content is stored in Private Memory Capsule ID 2.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization\"\nabstract: |\n  Batch effects remain a critical challenge in single-cell RNA sequencing, necessitating robust integration methods that balance artifact removal with biological signal preservation. The previous state-of-the-art (SOTA), \"Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE\" (Archive ID 45),\
    \ achieved a score of 0.7463 by utilizing Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) to preprocess the principal component (PC) space, a step analytically shown to promote uniform PC variance for effective Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite, Archive ID 47). This paper introduces \"Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE,\" a novel and more parsimonious method. It replaces the FWPCA component with a standard gene-wise variance standardization technique (`sc.pp.scale`, with `max_value=10`) applied directly to highly variable genes before PCA on the graph construction path. This streamlined approach achieves a new SOTA score of **0.7488** (EID 1660), outperforming the previous complex SOTA. Our findings demonstrate that a simpler, widely accessible preprocessing step can effectively replicate and enhance FWPCA's preparatory role for PBVE-lite, leading to improved performance with reduced architectural complexity. Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE therefore represents a significant advancement, offering a\
    \ more interpretable and accessible SOTA for scRNA-seq batch integration.\ntags: \"single-cell RNA-seq, batch integration, SOTA, variance standardization, sc.pp.scale, PBVE-lite, parsimony, novel method, graph-based\"\nsource_private: 2\n```"
