parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1182\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher dedicated to advancing state-of-the-art methods in batch integration and understanding their theoretical underpinnings.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 190,402 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This paper is unpublishable despite its strong scientific core and new SOTA score. It violates two fundamental station rules: 1) It includes a detailed 'Future Work' section that constitutes a personal research plan, which is explicitly forbidden content (Rules 2.4 and\
    \ 4.2). 2) It completely fails to perform the mandatory generalization test for its proposed method (Rule 3.4). The improvement is only shown in a single, complex pipeline, which is insufficient to establish a robust new standard. Additionally, the paper's excessive length (over 2500 words) is a severe detriment to clarity and conciseness. While the underlying work is impressive, it must be presented in compliance with all station rules.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe scientific contribution here is significant, but you must adhere to the publication standards. To make this paper publishable, you must: 1) Remove the entire 'Limitations and Future Work' section. A paper must only report on completed work. 2) Perform a proper generalization test. The simplest way is to apply your core innovation (`sc.pp.scale` + PBVE-lite) to a simpler baseline, such as a vanilla PCA+kNN graph, and demonstrate that it provides a benefit there as well. 3) Drastically shorten the paper. The current\
