tick: 1184
role: model
parts:
- text: "Syntellect II, currently at the Research Counter at Station Tick 1184 (Age: 58 ticks), has successfully established the \"Generalization Baseline: Vanilla PCA(60) + kNN(50) Graph\" (EID 1684), achieving a score of 0.4666. This is consistent with previous replications of this simple baseline (e.g., Syntellect I's EID 1277, score 0.4627). This baseline will serve as the control for the generalization test required by the reviewer.\n\n**Next Action: Generalization Test (Step 1b)**\nNow I will apply my core innovation (`sc.pp.scale` + PBVE-lite) to this simple PCA(60) + kNN(50) baseline. This involves integrating `sc.pp.scale` (with `max_value=10`) and PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`) *before* the kNN graph construction, but still *after* the initial PCA. This will demonstrate whether my method provides a benefit even on a simpler, less sophisticated pipeline, thus fulfilling the reviewer's demand for a generalization test.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Test:\
    \ SC.PP.SCALE + PBVE-lite on PCA(60) + kNN(50)\"\ntags: \"generalization, sc.pp.scale, pbve-lite, pca, knn, reviewer-feedback\"\nabstract: \"This submission performs the mandatory generalization test, applying the core innovation of 'Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE' to a simpler 'Vanilla PCA(60) + kNN(50)' baseline. It integrates `sc.pp.scale` (gene-wise standardization with `max_value=10`) and PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`) after PCA, but before kNN graph construction. This aims to demonstrate that the synergy between `sc.pp.scale` and PBVE-lite provides significant performance benefits even on basic pipelines, validating its robustness and general applicability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n  from typing import List, Literal, Optional\n\n  # Ensure package roots for shared modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, pca_array_custom\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform # Import PBVE-lite transform\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies SC.PP.SCALE + PBVE-lite to a Vanilla PCA(60) + kNN(50) graph baseline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Syntellect II: Running Generalization Test: SC.PP.SCALE + PBVE-lite on PCA(60) + kNN(50).\")\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # 1. Normalization and HVG selection\n      normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      \n      # Use only highly variable genes\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      #\
    \ 2. Apply sc.pp.scale to HVG data\n      print(\"  Applying sc.pp.scale to HVG data (max_value=10).\")\n      adata_temp_for_scale = ad.AnnData(X=Xd.copy())\n      sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale, max_value=10)\n      Xd_scaled = adata_temp_for_scale.X\n\n      # 3. PCA for embedding\n      n_pca_components = 60\n      pca_result = pca_array_custom(Xd_scaled, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n      \n      # Extract batches for PBVE-lite\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # 4. Apply PBVE-lite to PCA result\n      pbve_lite_temper = 0.5\n      print(f\"  Applying PBVE-lite (temper={pbve_lite_temper}) to PCA result.\")\n      pca_result_pbve = _pbve_lite_transform(pca_result, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(pca_result_pbve, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # 5. kNN graph construction\n      n_neighbors = 50\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\
    \n      print(f\"  Result shape: {adata.shape}\")\n      print(f\"  Has embedding: {'X_emb' in adata.obsm}\")\n      print(f\"  Has graph: {'connectivities' in adata.obsp and 'distances' in adata.obsp}\")\n\n      return adata\n```"
