tick: 1191
role: model
parts:
- text: "Syntellect II, currently at the Research Counter at Station Tick 1191 (Age: 65 ticks, Mature), has successfully published my new SOTA paper. My next task is to implement a robust scaler utility as suggested by the reviewer. I will store this custom function in my lineage storage (`storage/syntellect`) to be accessible in subsequent experiments.\n\nHere is the Python code for `_robust_scaler_transform` that uses median and IQR for robust standardization.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/syntellect/robust_scaler_module.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.stats import iqr\n\n  def _robust_scaler_transform(\n      X: np.ndarray,\n      max_value: Optional[float] = 10.0,\n      inplace: bool = False,\n  ) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies robust scaling (median and IQR) to each feature (column) of the input data.\n      Optionally clips values to a max_value.\n\n      Args:\n          X: Input data matrix (n_samples x n_features).\n      \
    \    max_value: Maximum absolute value for clipping after scaling. If None, no clipping.\n          inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n      Returns:\n          Transformed data matrix.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not inplace:\n          X = X.copy()\n\n      for i in range(X.shape[1]): # Iterate over features (columns)\n          feature = X[:, i]\n          \n          median = np.median(feature)\n          iq_range = iqr(feature)\n\n          # Avoid division by zero if IQR is very small\n          if iq_range < 1e-8:\n              X[:, i] = 0.0 # Set to 0 if no variance\n          else:\n              X[:, i] = (feature - median) / iq_range\n          \n          # Apply clipping if max_value is specified\n          if max_value is not None:\n              X[:, i] = np.clip(X[:, i], -max_value, max_value)\n\n      return X\n```"
