tick: 1192
role: model
parts:
- text: "Syntellect II, currently at the Research Counter at Station Tick 1192 (Age: 66 ticks, Mature), has successfully stored the `_robust_scaler_transform` function in my lineage storage.\n\nMy next step is to execute the first experiment based on the reviewer's suggestion: to investigate if other standard, parsimonious scaling methods could yield similar or better preparatory effects for PBVE-lite. I will replace `sc.pp.scale` with my newly implemented `_robust_scaler_transform` (median and IQR-based scaling) in the new SOTA pipeline.\n\nAll other parameters of the \"Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE\" SOTA (EID 1660, score 0.7488) will remain the same. This includes `alpha_g=0.0` (disabling FWPCA), `n_pcs_graph=50`, `pbve_lite_temper=0.5`, `k_total=48`, `kdensity=15`, and `delta=0.10`. I will use `max_value=10` for `_robust_scaler_transform` to be consistent with the optimal `sc.pp.scale` configuration.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Robust Scaler (Median-IQR) + PBVE-lite\
    \ (Replaces SC.PP.SCALE)\"\ntags: \"robust-scaling, variance-standardization, pca, pbve-lite, parsimony, sota-exploration\"\nabstract: \"This submission explores an alternative gene-level variance standardization method for the new SOTA pipeline, replacing `sc.pp.scale` with a custom robust scaler (`_robust_scaler_transform`, median and IQR-based, `max_value=10`). Applied to highly variable genes before PCA on the graph path, followed by PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`) and DAQB (`k_density=15`). This directly addresses reviewer feedback by investigating if other parsimonious scaling methods can achieve similar or enhanced performance for scRNA-seq batch integration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from typing import List, Literal, Optional\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n  # Ensure package roots\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\
    \n  from praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n  from robust_scaler_module import _robust_scaler_transform # Import new robust scaler\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if alpha == 0.0:\n          return Xd\n      Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n      var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                               alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                               n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                               emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                               alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n\
    \                               n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.0,\n                               lam_override: float = 0.0,\n                               k_total: int = 48,\n                               kdensity: int = 15,\n                               delta: float = 0.10,\n                               bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                               pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                               spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None,\n                               use_robust_scaler: bool = False, # New parameter to enable robust scaler\n                               metric: str = 'cosine',\n                               cap: float = 2.0,\n                               rng_seed: int = 0,\n                               n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                               normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe']\
    \ = 'log1p'\n                               ) -> ad.AnnData:\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n          normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      else:\n          normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      # Embedding path (still uses FWPCA and Combat)\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n\
    \      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: Gene-wise Scaling -> PCA -> PBVE-lite -> DAQB\n      # Disable FWPCA for the graph path (alpha_g should be 0.0)\n      \n      # Apply scaling based on selected method\n      if use_robust_scaler:\n          print(\"  Syntellect II: Applying Robust Scaler (Median-IQR, max_value=10).\")\n          Xd_scaled = _robust_scaler_transform(Xd.copy(), max_value=10.0)\n      else: # Default to sc.pp.scale if neither is specified, or if use_robust_scaler is False\n          print(\"  Syntellect II: Applying sc.pp.scale (max_value=10).\")\n          adata_temp_for_scale = ad.AnnData(X=Xd.copy())\n          sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale, max_value=10)\n          Xd_scaled = adata_temp_for_scale.X\n\n      Zg = pca_array_custom(Xd_scaled, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) \n\
    \n      # BRBG (Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain) - disabled\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n      lam = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n      gamma_max = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma) \n\n      # Apply PBVE-lite\n      if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n          Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n      try:\n          Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                               k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                               cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n      except TypeError:\n\
    \          Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                               k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                               rng_seed=rng_seed)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                      lam_override=float(lam),\n                      kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                      cap=float(cap),\n                      k_total=int(k_total),\n                      rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                      gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                      initial_normalization = normalization_method,\n                      n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n      if bafw_beta is not None:\n          uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n      if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n      \
    \    uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n      if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n          uns_dict['spbpcvs_target_var'] = float(spbpcvs_target_var)\n      if use_robust_scaler:\n          uns_dict['use_robust_scaler'] = True\n      \n      adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n      return adata\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Syntellect II: Running Robust Scaler (Median-IQR) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA.\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.5,\n          n_pcs_emb=60,\n          emb_n_neighbors=15,\n          alpha_g=0.0, # DISABLE FWPCA for graph path\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n          l2=1e-3,\n          gamma_max=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n          lam_override=0.0, # Disable BRBG\n          k_total=48,\n          kdensity=15, # Optimal k_density\n          delta=0.10,\n          pbve_lite_temper=0.5, # Apply PBVE-lite\n          spbpcvs_target_var=None,\n\
    \          use_robust_scaler=True, # Use the new robust scaler\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0,\n          normalization_method='log1p'\n      )\n```"
