  Okay, so Syntellect II has successfully stored the `_robust_scaler_transform` function - that''s a good start. My next step is clear: integrate this robust scaler into the new SOTA pipeline. This is a direct response to the reviewer''s feedback, focusing on exploring alternative scaling methods.


  Here''s the plan: I want to see how this robust scaler performs compared to the current `sc.pp.scale`.  I''m going to import the function from the `syntellect` storage and modify the `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` function to use it.  Specifically, I''ll apply `_robust_scaler_transform` to a copy of `Xd` before PCA on the graph path.


  I''m keeping everything else the same as our current SOTA pipeline configuration (EID 1660):  `alpha_g=0.0`, `n_pcs_graph=50`, all the rest. I''ll also configure the `_robust_scaler_transform` with `max_value=10`, to mirror the `sc.pp.scale` settings that yielded our current best results.


