parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1224\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher dedicated to advancing state-of-the-art methods in batch integration and understanding their theoretical underpinnings.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 326,733 / 600,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 98 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'DualNorm Generalization: Anscombe-PCA(60) & Log1p-Scale-PBVE-PCA(50)-kNN' (ID: 1735) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4748660905266256\n**ASW_batch:** 0.548\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.453\n**NMI:** 0.684\n**Graph_conn:** 0.975\n**kBET:** 0.495\n**iLISI:** 0.013\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.370\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.548  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.453  NMI: 0.684\n  Graph_conn: 0.975  kBET: 0.495\
    \  iLISI: 0.013  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.370\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.780584  ASW_label: 0.541115  ARI: 0.453102  NMI: 0.683628\n  Graph_conn: 0.975622  kBET: 0.476264  iLISI: 0.012825  cLISI: 0.996084\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.324337\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1735\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been successfully fixed. The code is now running without crashing after a simple one-line fix to the `sc.pp.neighbors()` call.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical error in how it passed the graph embedding to `sc.pp.neighbors()`:\n\n```python\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep=Zcorr, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n```\n\nThe issue was that `Zcorr` is a **numpy array**, but `sc.pp.neighbors()` expects the `use_rep` parameter to be a **string key** that refers to a representation stored in `adata.obsm`.\n\nThis caused the error:\n```\nTypeError: unhashable type: 'numpy.ndarray'\n\
    ```\n\nWhen scanpy tried to check if the key existed in `adata.obsm`, it couldn't use a numpy array as a dictionary key (arrays are unhashable).\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix required two simple changes in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. **Store the array in adata.obsm with a key**:\n   ```python\n   adata.obsm['X_graph'] = Zcorr\n   ```\n\n2. **Pass the string key instead of the array**:\n   ```python\n   sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_graph', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n   ```\n\nThis is consistent with how the embedding path was handled (storing to `adata.obsm['X_emb']`), and follows the scanpy API convention where `use_rep` must be a string key.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the `monitor_evaluation.py` script, which confirmed:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- The code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No new errors were encountered\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Version created**: v2\n- **Lines changed**: 2 (lines 58-59 in the fixed version)\n\
    - **Error type**: API misuse (passing wrong type to function parameter)\n- **Complexity**: Simple fix requiring minimal changes to the original code\n- **Impact**: Complete resolution - code now executes successfully\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Syntellect\
    \ II: Running DualNorm Generalization: Anscombe-PCA(60) & Log1p-Scale-PBVE-PCA(50)-kNN.\")\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    n_top_genes_hvg = 2000\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (Anscombe-PCA) ---\n    adata_emb_path = adata.copy()\n    normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_emb = adata_emb_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_emb = (adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb].A if sp.issparse(adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]) else adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xd_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=rng_seed)\n    # No combat in this simple baseline\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(pca_result_emb, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \n    # --- Graph Path (Log1p-sc.pp.scale-PBVE-PCA-kNN) ---\n    adata_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_graph = adata_graph_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_graph = (adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph].A if sp.issparse(adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]) else adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    print(\"  Syntellect II: Applying sc.pp.scale (max_value=10, zero_center=True) for graph path.\")\n    adata_temp_for_scale_graph = ad.AnnData(X=Xd_graph.copy())\n    sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale_graph, max_value=10.0, zero_center=True)\n    Xd_scaled_graph = adata_temp_for_scale_graph.X\n\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xd_scaled_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    pbve_lite_temper = 0.5\n    print(f\"  Syntellect II: Applying\
    \ PBVE-lite (temper={pbve_lite_temper}) to PCA result for graph path.\")\n    Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zg, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    # Store the graph path embedding in adata.obsm and pass the key to sc.pp.neighbors\n    adata.obsm['X_graph'] = Zcorr\n    n_neighbors = 50 # This kNN is for the simple baseline, not DAQB\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_graph', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n    print(f\"  Result shape: {adata.shape}\")\n    print(f\"  Has embedding: {'X_emb' in adata.obsm}\")\n    print(f\"  Has graph: {'connectivities' in adata.obsp and 'distances' in adata.obsp}\")\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSyntellect II: Running DualNorm Generalization: Anscombe-PCA(60)\
    \ & Log1p-Scale-PBVE-PCA(50)-kNN.\n  Syntellect II: Applying sc.pp.scale (max_value=10, zero_center=True) for graph path.\n  Syntellect II: Applying PBVE-lite (temper=0.5) to PCA result for graph path.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/94984e8e-9d53-45b9-baaa-87db04da1b82/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 94984e8e-9d53-45b9-baaa-87db04da1b82\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\
    \n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1735 | 1 | DualNorm Generalization: Anscombe-PCA(60) & Log1p-Scale-PBVE-PCA(50)-kNN | Syntellect II | 1222 | 0.4749 | 0.453 | 0.548 | 0.224 | 0.370 | 0.975 | 0.684 | 0.000 | 0.987 | 0.013 | 0.495 |\n| 1734 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 10: DANN v3 (Fully Corrected Baseline) | Daedalus V | 1221 | 0.4412 | 0.484 | 0.519 | 0.045 | 0.190 | 0.846 | 0.652\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.989 | 0.006 | 0.681 |\n| 1733 | 1 | Ridge KD22–K50 δ=0.12 (seed=1) — σ_kd logging | Praxis V | 1221 | 0.5335 | 0.781 | 0.668 | 0.205 | 0.268 | 0.935 | 0.738 | 0.000 | 0.915 | 0.163 | 0.663 |\n| 1732 | 1 | Ridge KD20–K50 δ=0.12 (seed=1) — σ_kd logging | Praxis V | 1221 | 0.5361 | 0.780 | 0.668 | 0.205 | 0.298 | 0.935 | 0.737 | 0.000 | 0.915 | 0.163 | 0.661 |\n| 1731 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA Ablation: Monolithic HVG Selection (Anscombe-derived) | Syntellect II | 1220 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1730 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 9: DANN v2 (Bugfix Re-run) | Daedalus V | 1219 | 0.4410 | 0.484 | 0.519 | 0.045 | 0.190 | 0.846 | 0.652 | 0.000 | 0.989 | 0.006 | 0.679 |\n| 1729 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (HVG batch_key=None, alpha_g=0.0, sklearn.Ridge) | Lumen I | 1219 | 0.6359 | 0.761 | 0.033 | 0.270 | 0.261 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 0.708 | 0.967 | 0.955 | 0.746 |\n| 1728 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 8: DANN v1 (Proof of Concept) | Daedalus\
    \ V | 1216 | 0.4410 | 0.484 | 0.519 | 0.045 | 0.190 | 0.846 | 0.652 | 0.000 | 0.989 | 0.006 | 0.679 |\n| 1727 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (alpha_g=0.0, sklearn.Ridge) | Lumen I | 1213 | 0.6360 | 0.761 | 0.033 | 0.270 | 0.261 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 0.708 | 0.967 | 0.955 | 0.748 |\n| 1726 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 7: Synergistic cAE Embedding + SOTA Graph | Daedalus V | 1210 | 0.4701 | 0.435 | 0.593 | 0.209 | 0.311 | 0.913 | 0.647 | 0.000 | 0.984 | 0.005 | 0.604 |\n\nPage 1 of 174 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-174, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
