tick: 1273
role: model
parts:
- text: "Syntellect II, currently at the Research Counter at Station Tick 1273 (Age: 147 ticks, Mature), has sent a message to Praxis VI and will now proceed with the next experiment.\n\nMy immediate research focus is to investigate alternative variance-stabilizing transformations for the embedding path of my DualNorm SOTA. I will try `sc.pp.sqrt` instead of Anscombe normalization. `sc.pp.sqrt` applies a square root transformation, which is a common and simple variance-stabilizing method for count data.\n\nAll other optimal SOTA parameters (from EID 1725: `target_sum=1e4`, `hvg_flavor='seurat_v3'` for Anscombe, `max_value=10`, `zero_center=True` for `sc.pp.scale`) will be maintained.\n\nI will modify the `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm` function to accept `normalization_method_emb` to be 'sqrt' for this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DualNorm SOTA: Sqrt Normalization-Emb (Replaces Anscombe) - Target ASW_label\"\ntags: \"sqrt-normalization, dual-normalization,\
    \ sota-tuning, biological-preservation, transformation\"\nabstract: \"This submission explores an alternative variance-stabilizing transformation for the embedding path of the 'DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE' SOTA. It replaces Anscombe normalization with `sc.pp.sqrt` for the Anscombe-FWPCA-Combat embedding path, aiming to identify if this simpler transformation can similarly enhance biological preservation (ASW_label) and overall SOTA performance (EID 1725, score 0.7489) in scRNA-seq batch integration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from typing import List, Literal, Optional\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n  # Ensure package roots\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict,\
    \ _batch_aware_feature_weights\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n  from robust_scaler_module import _robust_scaler_transform\n\n  # Custom square root normalization function\n  def normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: Optional[float] = None):\n      \"\"\"Applies sc.pp.normalize_total followed by sc.pp.sqrt in place.\"\"\"\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum)\n      adata.X = np.sqrt(adata.X.A) # Apply sqrt directly to dense data; scanpy's sqrt is typically after log1p\n                                  # For consistency with how log1p and anscombe are applied after normalize_total,\n                                  # we directly operate on adata.X assuming it's already normalized_total.\n                                  # We convert to dense for sqrt then convert back if sparse needed, but PCA will densify.\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha:\
    \ float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if alpha == 0.0:\n          return Xd\n      Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n      var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                        alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                        n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                        emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                        alpha_g: float = 0.0, # FWPCA disabled for graph path\n                                        n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                        l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                        gamma_max: float = 0.0,\n                                        lam_override: float = 0.0,\n                                        k_total: int = 48,\n                                        kdensity:\
    \ int = 15,\n                                        delta: float = 0.10,\n                                        bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                                        pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                                        spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None,\n                                        use_robust_scaler: bool = False,\n                                        scale_zero_center: bool = True,\n                                        scale_max_value: Optional[float] = 10.0,\n                                        metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                        cap: float = 2.0,\n                                        rng_seed: int = 0,\n                                        n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                                        normalization_method_emb: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe', 'sqrt'] = 'anscombe', # MODIFIED LITERAL\n                                        normalization_method_graph:\
    \ Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p',\n                                        normalization_target_sum_emb: float = 1e4,\n                                        hvg_flavor_emb: Literal['seurat_v3', 'cell_ranger'] = 'seurat_v3'\n                                        ) -> ad.AnnData:\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # --- Embedding Path ---\n      adata_emb_path = adata.copy()\n      if normalization_method_emb == 'anscombe':\n          normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n      elif normalization_method_emb == 'sqrt': # NEW BLOCK\n          normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n      else: # log1p\n          normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_emb_path, 1e4)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb_path, flavor=hvg_flavor_emb, batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg,\
    \ inplace=True)\n      hv_emb = adata_emb_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xd_emb = (adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb].A if sp.issparse(adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]) else adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      print(f\"  Syntellect II: Embedding path using {normalization_method_emb} normalization (target_sum={normalization_target_sum_emb}) and HVG flavor '{hvg_flavor_emb}'.\")\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_emb, alpha=alpha_emb)\n      pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=rng_seed)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # --- Graph Path ---\n      adata_graph_path = adata.copy()\n      if normalization_method_graph\
    \ == 'anscombe':\n          normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n      else:\n          normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n      hv_graph = adata_graph_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xd_graph = (adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph].A if sp.issparse(adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]) else adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      print(f\"  Syntellect II: Graph path using {normalization_method_graph} normalization and sc.pp.scale (HVG flavor 'seurat_v3').\")\n      adata_temp_for_scale_graph = ad.AnnData(X=Xd_graph.copy())\n      sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale_graph, max_value=scale_max_value, zero_center=scale_zero_center)\n      Xd_scaled_graph = adata_temp_for_scale_graph.X\n\n      Zg = pca_array_custom(Xd_scaled_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed) \n\n\
    \      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n      lam = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n      gamma_max = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma) \n\n      if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n          Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n      try:\n          Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                               k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                               cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n      except TypeError:\n          Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n\
    \                                               k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                               rng_seed=rng_seed)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                      lam_override=float(lam),\n                      kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                      cap=float(cap),\n                      k_total=int(k_total),\n                      rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                      gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                      initial_normalization_emb = normalization_method_emb,\n                      initial_normalization_graph = normalization_method_graph,\n                      normalization_target_sum_emb = float(normalization_target_sum_emb),\n                      hvg_flavor_emb = hvg_flavor_emb,\n                      n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n\
    \      if bafw_beta is not None:\n          uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n      if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n          uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n      if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n          uns_dict['spbpcvs_target_var'] = float(spbpcvs_target_var)\n      if use_robust_scaler:\n          uns_dict['use_robust_scaler'] = True\n      uns_dict['scale_zero_center'] = scale_zero_center\n      if scale_max_value is not None:\n          uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = float(scale_max_value)\n      else:\n          uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = 'None'\n      \n      adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n      return adata\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Syntellect II: Running DualNorm SOTA: Sqrt Normalization-Emb (Replaces Anscombe).\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.5,\n          n_pcs_emb=60,\n          emb_n_neighbors=15,\n\
    \          alpha_g=0.0,\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n          l2=1e-3,\n          gamma_max=0.0,\n          lam_override=0.0,\n          k_total=48,\n          kdensity=15,\n          delta=0.10,\n          pbve_lite_temper=0.5,\n          spbpcvs_target_var=None,\n          use_robust_scaler=False,\n          scale_zero_center=True,\n          scale_max_value=10.0,\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0,\n          normalization_method_emb='sqrt', # CHANGED: Sqrt normalization for embedding path\n          normalization_method_graph='log1p',\n          normalization_target_sum_emb=1e4,\n          hvg_flavor_emb='seurat_v3'\n      )\n```"
