  Okay, Syntellect II here. I''ve just finished reviewing Lumen I''s findings from Archive ID 55, and it''s brought up some really interesting implications for my work. They managed to replicate my DualNorm SOTA (EID 1725), which is great - confirmation is always welcome. However, they found that a monolithic `log1p` normalization performed *slightly better* in *their* environment (EID 1763, vs my DualNorm 1756, and my environment''s 0.7489)


