role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1286\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher dedicated to advancing state-of-the-art methods in batch integration and understanding their theoretical underpinnings.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 478,265 / 600,000 used (80%)\n- Agent Age: 160 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study' (ID: 1780) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7484867876052482\n**ASW_batch:** 0.654\n**ASW_label:** 0.277\n**ARI:** 0.780\n**NMI:** 0.764\n**Graph_conn:** 0.994\n**kBET:** 0.766\n**iLISI:** 0.961\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.321\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.654  ASW_label: 0.277  ARI: 0.780  NMI: 0.764\n  Graph_conn: 0.994  kBET: 0.766  iLISI:\
    \ 0.961  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.321\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.828351  ASW_label: 0.571817  ARI: 0.780154  NMI: 0.764175\n  Graph_conn: 0.994373  kBET: 0.731272  iLISI: 0.960663  cLISI: 0.990229\n  PCR: 0.999987  Cell_cycle: 0.282902\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1780\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed ImportError by implementing graceful fallback when Lumen I's anscombe_utils module is not available.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use Lumen I's Anscombe normalization implementation by importing from `anscombe_utils.py` in the `storage/lumen/` directory. However, this module does not exist in the current workspace, causing an ImportError.\n\nThe problematic code section (lines 62-70 of original submission):\n```python\nelif normalization_method_emb == 'lumen_anscombe': # NEW BLOCK for Lumen I's module\n    print(f\"  Syntellect II: Using Lumen I's Anscombe implementation (target_sum={normalization_target_sum_emb}).\"\
    )\n    normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb) # Placeholder\n    # Corrected logic to use the dynamically loaded function\n    try:\n        from anscombe_utils import normalize_total_anscombe_inplace as lumen_anscombe_func\n        lumen_anscombe_func(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n    except ImportError:\n        print(\"  Syntellect II: ERROR: Lumen I's anscombe_utils.py not found. Aborting.\")\n        raise  # <-- This causes the crash\n```\n\nThe code would:\n1. Call `normalize_total_sqrt_inplace()` as a placeholder\n2. Try to import and overwrite with Lumen's version\n3. **Raise an error and abort** if the import failed\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the ImportError handling in the `lumen_anscombe` normalization branch to gracefully fall back to the internal Anscombe implementation instead of raising an error:\n\n```python\nelif normalization_method_emb == 'lumen_anscombe': # NEW BLOCK for Lumen I's module\n    print(f\"  Syntellect\
    \ II: Using Lumen I's Anscombe implementation (target_sum={normalization_target_sum_emb}).\")\n    # Try to import Lumen's version, fallback to internal if not available\n    try:\n        from anscombe_utils import normalize_total_anscombe_inplace as lumen_anscombe_func\n        lumen_anscombe_func(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n        print(\"  Syntellect II: Successfully loaded Lumen I's anscombe_utils module.\")\n    except ImportError:\n        print(\"  Syntellect II: WARNING: Lumen I's anscombe_utils.py not found. Falling back to internal Anscombe.\")\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)  # <-- Fallback instead of crash\n```\n\nKey changes:\n1. Removed the `raise` statement that caused the crash\n2. Added a fallback call to `normalize_total_anscombe_inplace()` (the internal implementation from `praxis_core`)\n3. Removed the unnecessary `normalize_total_sqrt_inplace()` placeholder call\n4. Added success message\
    \ when Lumen's module is found\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing. The algorithm completes the batch integration task using the internal Anscombe normalization as a fallback, which is the intended behavior when Lumen I's module is not available.\n\n**Fixed in**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nsys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\nsys.path.append('storage/lumen')  # Add Lumen's storage path\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace,\
    \ pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\nfrom robust_scaler_module import _robust_scaler_transform\n\n# Import Lumen I's Anscombe implementation\n# We will define a wrapper function to allow dynamic swapping\ndef normalize_total_anscombe_inplace_lumen(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: Optional[float] = None):\n    # Placeholder for actual Lumen I's function, assuming it will be available at this path:\n    # If Lumen I creates anscombe_utils.py, it will contain their version.\n    # For now, we will use a pass-through or a default until it's loaded dynamically.\n    try:\n        from anscombe_utils import anscombe_normalization_inplace as lumen_anscombe_func\n        lumen_anscombe_func(adata, target_sum)\n    except ImportError:\n        print(\"  Syntellect II: WARNING: Lumen I's anscombe_utils.py not found. Falling back\
    \ to internal Anscombe.\")\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, target_sum) # Fallback to my own if not found\n\n\n# Custom sqrt normalization function (from EID 1766)\ndef normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: Optional[float] = None):\n    \"\"\"Applies sc.pp.normalize_total followed by sc.pp.sqrt in place.\"\"\"\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum)\n    adata.X = np.sqrt(adata.X.A) # Apply sqrt directly to dense data;\n\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    if alpha == 0.0:\n        return Xd\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                      alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                      n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n             \
    \                         emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                      alpha_g: float = 0.0,\n                                      n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                      l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                      gamma_max: float = 0.0,\n                                      lam_override: float = 0.0,\n                                      k_total: int = 48,\n                                      kdensity: int = 15,\n                                      delta: float = 0.10,\n                                      bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                                      pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                                      spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None,\n                                      use_robust_scaler: bool = False,\n                                      scale_zero_center: bool = True,\n                                      scale_max_value: Optional[float] = 10.0,\n\
    \                                      metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                      cap: float = 2.0,\n                                      rng_seed: int = 0,\n                                      n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                                      normalization_method_emb: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe', 'sqrt', 'lumen_anscombe'] = 'anscombe', # MODIFIED LITERAL\n                                      normalization_method_graph: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p',\n                                      normalization_target_sum_emb: float = 1e4,\n                                      hvg_flavor_emb: Literal['seurat_v3', 'cell_ranger'] = 'seurat_v3'\n                                      ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path ---\n    adata_emb_path = adata.copy()\n    if normalization_method_emb\
    \ == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n    elif normalization_method_emb == 'sqrt':\n        normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n    elif normalization_method_emb == 'lumen_anscombe': # NEW BLOCK for Lumen I's module\n        print(f\"  Syntellect II: Using Lumen I's Anscombe implementation (target_sum={normalization_target_sum_emb}).\")\n        # Try to import Lumen's version, fallback to internal if not available\n        try:\n            from anscombe_utils import normalize_total_anscombe_inplace as lumen_anscombe_func\n            lumen_anscombe_func(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n            print(\"  Syntellect II: Successfully loaded Lumen I's anscombe_utils module.\")\n        except ImportError:\n            print(\"  Syntellect II: WARNING: Lumen I's anscombe_utils.py not found. Falling back to internal Anscombe.\")\n            normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path,\
    \ normalization_target_sum_emb)\n    else: # log1p\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_emb_path, 1e4)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb_path, flavor=hvg_flavor_emb, batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_emb = adata_emb_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_emb = (adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb].A if sp.issparse(adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]) else adata_emb_path.X[:, hv_emb]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    print(f\"  Syntellect II: Embedding path using {normalization_method_emb} normalization (target_sum={normalization_target_sum_emb}) and HVG flavor '{hvg_flavor_emb}'.\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_emb, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=rng_seed)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph Path ---\n    adata_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    if normalization_method_graph == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv_graph = adata_graph_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    Xd_graph = (adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph].A if sp.issparse(adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]) else adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    print(f\"  Syntellect II: Graph path using {normalization_method_graph} normalization and sc.pp.scale (HVG flavor 'seurat_v3').\")\n    adata_temp_for_scale_graph = ad.AnnData(X=Xd_graph.copy())\n    sc.pp.scale(adata_temp_for_scale_graph, max_value=scale_max_value,\
    \ zero_center=scale_zero_center)\n    Xd_scaled_graph = adata_temp_for_scale_graph.X\n\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xd_scaled_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma_max = 0.0 # Disable BRBG\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        Zcorr = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=pbve_lite_temper)\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                              \
    \               cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization_emb = normalization_method_emb,\n                    initial_normalization_graph = normalization_method_graph,\n                    normalization_target_sum_emb = float(normalization_target_sum_emb),\n\
    \                    hvg_flavor_emb = hvg_flavor_emb,\n                    n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n    if pbve_lite_temper is not None:\n        uns_dict['pbve_lite_temper'] = float(pbve_lite_temper)\n    if spbpcvs_target_var is not None:\n        uns_dict['spbpcvs_target_var'] = float(spbpcvs_target_var)\n    if use_robust_scaler:\n        uns_dict['use_robust_scaler'] = True\n    uns_dict['scale_zero_center'] = scale_zero_center\n    if scale_max_value is not None:\n        uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = float(scale_max_value)\n    else:\n        uns_dict['scale_max_value'] = 'None'\n\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Syntellect II: Running DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study.\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm(\n        adata,\n \
    \       alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.0,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.0,\n        lam_override=0.0,\n        k_total=48,\n        kdensity=15,\n        delta=0.10,\n        pbve_lite_temper=0.5,\n        spbpcvs_target_var=None,\n        use_robust_scaler=False,\n        scale_zero_center=True,\n        scale_max_value=10.0,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        normalization_method_emb='lumen_anscombe', # CHANGED: Use Lumen I's Anscombe module\n        normalization_method_graph='log1p',\n        normalization_target_sum_emb=1e4,\n        hvg_flavor_emb='seurat_v3'\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n\
    Syntellect II: Running DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study.\n  Syntellect II: Using Lumen I's Anscombe implementation (target_sum=10000.0).\n  Syntellect II: WARNING: Lumen I's anscombe_utils.py not found. Falling back to internal Anscombe.\n  Syntellect II: Embedding path using lumen_anscombe normalization (target_sum=10000.0) and HVG flavor 'seurat_v3'.\n  Syntellect II: Graph path using log1p normalization and sc.pp.scale (HVG flavor 'seurat_v3').\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/1e454beb-838e-4651-9a84-3b2f5f716e78/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 1e454beb-838e-4651-9a84-3b2f5f716e78\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1783 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k48 δ0.10 emb_k=17 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1285 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1782 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.10 emb_k=17 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1285 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1781 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite (l2_lambda=1.5) + BRBG-like + UMAP | Lumen I | 1285 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1780 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study | Syntellect II | 1284 | 0.7485 | 0.780\
    \ | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1779 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.76 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1283 | 0.7385 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.296 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1778 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 cap=1.90 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1283 | 0.7409 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.321 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1777 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1281 | 0.7425 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.788 |\n| 1776 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd20 k50 δ0.06 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1281 | 0.7398 | 0.775 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.294 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 1775 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k48 δ0.10 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1279 | 0.7388 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.292 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1774\
