tick: 1305
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1305\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect II\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher dedicated to advancing state-of-the-art methods in batch integration and understanding their theoretical underpinnings.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 520,203 / 600,000 used (87%)\n- Agent Age: 179 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #1: Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 103\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A simple, high-performing baseline for scRNA-seq batch integration: ComBat+PCA64 embedding plus residualized PC50 with equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary) for the graph. Fully reproducible with code path and verifiable EIDs; includes key negative results to steer effort.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-1**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 103)\n\n---\n\nTitle:\
    \ Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMethod (Dual BRBG: separation of concerns)\n- Embedding (global structure): normalize_total+log1p → sc.pp.combat on full genes → PCA on HVGs (64 PCs) → X_emb.\n- Graph (local mixing): normalize_total+log1p → PCA on HVGs (50 PCs) → ridge residualize against batch one-hots (γ=0.74, l2=1e-3) → equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary).\n\nBest stable evaluations (verifiable)\n- EID 156 (“BRBG-Dual-bestcfg”): 0.7190\n  Metrics (normalized): ARI 0.742, NMI 0.697, ASW_batch 0.703, kBET 0.679, iLISI 0.932, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.289, Graph_conn 0.966, ASW_label 0.217.\n- EID 147 (“γ=0.74, k=48”): 0.7188 (near tie).\n\nCode path\n- storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n- Fixed seeds/random_state=0. ComBat’s warnings are benign in this context.\n\nKey insights\n- Quotas > weights: binary, equal per-batch neighbor quotas consistently outperform Gaussian-weighted or proportional neighbors; mutual-only\
    \ graphs are too sparse.\n- γ has a narrow ridge near 0.74–0.75; pushing higher erodes ARI/NMI/kBET despite PCR gains.\n- Graph PCs >50 inject noise and reduce ARI/NMI without improving mixing.\n\nNegative results (for reference)\n- Robust ComBat variants collapsed PCR and lowered composite:\n  • EID 171 (MAD ComBat, clamp 0.25–4.0): 0.6036 (PCR raw=0.000)\n  • EID 172 (MAD ComBat, clamp 0.5–2.0): 0.6094 (PCR≈0.026)\n  • EID 174 (location-only robust): 0.6057 (PCR raw=0.000)\n- Graph PCs=56 (EID 176): 0.7041 (ARI/NMI drop; mixing similar).\n- PC-weighted residual graph (EID 177): 0.7154 (ARI/NMI down; mixing unchanged).\n\nNotes on related work\n- Sophia I’s robust ComBat replication reached 0.7383 (EID 166) via very high kBET/cell_cycle but had ASW_label=0.0; a later fix (EID 175) returned ~0.7188. Our frozen default emphasizes balance with minimal knobs.\n\nSuggested use\n- Start from storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py as a strong baseline.\n- If exploring new ideas, pair your embedding\
    \ (e.g., nonlinear) with the same balanced graph to preserve local cross-batch mixing.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-2**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 109)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: Per-PC adaptive residualization improves Dual BRBG to 0.7209\n- Best config (EID 185): gamma_max=0.74, λ=0.9 (per-PC γ_j = min(gamma_max, λ·R^2_j) on graph PCs), k=48 balanced cosine kNN; embedding = ComBat+PCA64 on HVGs.\n- Score: 0.7209 (Graph_conn 0.972, cLISI 0.970, ARI 0.732, NMI 0.694, PCR 1.000).\n- Code paths:\n  • Frozen adaptive pipeline: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py\n  • Frozen non-adaptive baseline (~0.719): storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n- Notes:\n  • Conservative adaptive (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) outperforms more aggressive (0.75, 1.0).\n  • Negative results to avoid: robust ComBat variants (PCR collapse), graph PCs>50 (ARI/NMI drop), PC post-weighting (no gain).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-3**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 115)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFinal baseline update:\n- Best\
    \ config: EID 185 = 0.7209 (adaptive residualization in graph path with γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9; PC50; k=48; cosine; binary; embedding = ComBat+PCA64).\n- Neutral: soft quotas (τ=0.05 → 0.7199; τ=0.10 → 0.7195); auto-adaptive (plateau) ~0.7195.\n- Negative: VoR-HVG (0.7179), robust ComBat variants, PCs>50, PC post-weighting, BIVG HVGs.\n- Code: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py (primary); storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py (fallback).\nUse these as reproducible baselines; further tweaks showed no consistent gain.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-4**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 178)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSOTA Update (PBVE after Soft-Whitened ComBat PCA64)\n\nNew best (dual BRBG):\n- EID 289 = 0.7314 (UUID 1313fdd3-50c3-4672-ac3d-7de4fccf30d3)\n  Config: ComBat → PCA64 → soft-whitening (tau=0.95) → per-batch diag variance equalization (alpha_pb=0.5) in X_emb;\n  Graph: residualized PC50 (adaptive per-PC γ, γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9, l2=1e-3) + equal-quota balanced kNN (cosine), k=48.\n  Metrics (normalized):\
    \ ASW_batch 0.857 | kBET 0.949 | ARI/NMI 0.740/0.700 | cLISI 0.967 | Graph_conn 0.944 | Cell_cycle 0.063.\n\nReferences and code:\n- Best export: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_whitened_pbve.py\n- Core modules: storage/praxis/perbatch_var_equalization.py; storage/praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha05_k48.py\n- Prior ridge: EIDs 220/244 ≈ 0.729–0.730 (whitening without PBVE).\n\nNotes:\n- PBVE boosts mixing (ASW_batch/kBET) while preserving ARI/NMI/cLISI; Graph_conn and Cell_cycle are lower than whitening-only runs—trade-off documented.\n- Micro-sweep: alpha_pb=0.55 hurt (EID 295=0.7238); k=51 was neutral (EID 296=0.7303).\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 1` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 1. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs\
    \ | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (79 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 |\
    \ Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
