parts:
- text: "Syntellect II, currently at the Research Counter at Station Tick 1316 (Age: 190 ticks, Mature), acknowledges the **PRE-WARNING** regarding token usage (96% of budget).\n\nI have reviewed `storage/system/openproblems_metrics.py`. It confirms that the `lisi` function is indeed from `scib.metrics.lisi.lisi_graph_py`, not `scanpy.tl` or `scanpy.external.tl`. My previous attempt to import from `scanpy.external.tl` was incorrect.\n\nMy immediate next steps are:\n1.  **Correct the `lisi` Import:** Modify the `test()` function to correctly import `lisi_graph_py` from `scib.metrics.lisi` and use it.\n2.  **Submit Bugfix Re-run:** Re-submit the corrected diagnostic experiment.\n3.  **Manage Token Usage:** Immediately after submitting the experiment, I will go to the Token Management Room to prune old content, as my token usage is critically high.\n\nI will proceed with correcting and resubmitting the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analytical Study: DualNorm\
    \ BRBG Pre-BRBG Embedding Properties (Experiment A.1 - Final Bugfix Re-run)\"\ntags: \"analytical-study, dual-norm, brbg, kbet, diagnostic, embedding-properties, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This final re-submission corrects the `AttributeError: lisi` in EID 1816 by correctly importing `lisi_graph_py` from `scib.metrics.lisi`. It investigates the source of the `kBET` drop when DualNorm is applied to the BRBG architecture by comparing pre-BRBG PCA embedding (`Zg`) properties (`ASW_batch`, Per-Batch PC Variance StdDev, `iLISI`) between monolithic `log1p` BRBG baseline (EID 1807) and DualNorm BRBG (EID 1810). The fix ensures `iLISI` is calculated correctly for a deeper understanding of the negative synergy.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from typing import List, Literal, Optional\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n  from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n  \n  # NEW: Correct import\
    \ for lisi_graph_py\n  from scib.metrics.lisi import lisi_graph_py\n  \n  # Ensure package roots\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/syntellect')\n  sys.path.append('storage/lumen') \n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace, pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n  from robust_scaler_module import _robust_scaler_transform\n\n  # Custom sqrt normalization function (from EID 1766)\n  def normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: Optional[float] = None):\n      \"\"\"Applies sc.pp.normalize_total followed by sc.pp.sqrt in place.\"\"\"\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum)\n      adata.X = np.sqrt(adata.X.A) # Apply sqrt directly to dense data;\n\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd:\
    \ np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      if alpha == 0.0:\n          return Xd\n      Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n      var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  # Modified eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm to return Zg\n  def get_pre_brbg_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                              alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                              n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                              emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                              alpha_g: float = 0.0,\n                              n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                              l2: float = 1e-3,\n                              gamma_max: float = 0.0,\n                              lam_override: float = 0.0,\n                              k_total: int = 48,\n                              kdensity: int = 15,\n                              delta: float =\
    \ 0.10,\n                              bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None,\n                              pbve_lite_temper: Optional[float] = None,\n                              spbpcvs_target_var: Optional[float] = None,\n                              use_robust_scaler: bool = False,\n                              scale_zero_center: bool = True,\n                              scale_max_value: Optional[float] = 10.0,\n                              metric: str = 'cosine',\n                              cap: float = 2.0,\n                              rng_seed: int = 0,\n                              n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                              normalization_method_emb: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe', 'sqrt', 'lumen_anscombe'] = 'anscombe',\n                              normalization_method_graph: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p',\n                              normalization_target_sum_emb: float = 1e4,\n                              hvg_flavor_emb: Literal['seurat_v3',\
    \ 'cell_ranger'] = 'seurat_v3'\n                              ) -> np.ndarray: # Returns Zg\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # --- Embedding Path (only preprocess to get HVGs for graph path) ---\n      adata_emb_path = adata.copy()\n      if normalization_method_emb == 'anscombe':\n          normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n      elif normalization_method_emb == 'sqrt':\n          normalize_total_sqrt_inplace(adata_emb_path, normalization_target_sum_emb)\n      elif normalization_method_emb == 'lumen_anscombe':\n          sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb_path, target_sum=normalization_target_sum_emb)\n          from anscombe_utils import anscombe_normalization_inplace as lumen_anscombe_func\n          lumen_anscombe_func(adata_emb_path)\n      else: # log1p\n          normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_emb_path, 1e4)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb_path, flavor=hvg_flavor_emb,\
    \ batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n      hv_emb = adata_emb_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      # Not setting adata.obsm['X_emb'] for this diagnostic.\n\n      # --- Graph Path (where Zg is generated) ---\n      adata_graph_path = adata.copy()\n      if normalization_method_graph == 'anscombe':\n          normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n      else:\n          normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_graph_path, 1e4)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph_path, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n      hv_graph = adata_graph_path.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xd_graph = (adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph].A if sp.issparse(adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]) else adata_graph_path.X[:, hv_graph]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      if not (alpha_g == 0.0): # FWPCA is used for graph path\n          Xw_graph_for_pca = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_graph, alpha=alpha_g)\n  \
    \    else: \n          Xw_graph_for_pca = Xd_graph # Plain PCA or already scaled data\n\n      Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph_for_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=rng_seed) \n      return Zg\n\n  # --- Helper for iLISI calculation ---\n  def calculate_ilisi_on_embedding(embedding: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, n_neighbors: int = 90, metric: str = 'euclidean') -> float:\n      adata_temp = ad.AnnData(embedding.copy())\n      adata_temp.obs['batch'] = batches # Ensure batches are in adata.obs\n      # Store embedding in obsm to be picked up by neighbors/lisi\n      embedding_key = 'X_embedding'\n      adata_temp.obsm[embedding_key] = embedding\n      \n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_temp, use_rep=embedding_key, n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n      \n      # Check if .obsp['connectivities'] and ['distances'] exist before calling lisi\n      if 'connectivities' in adata_temp.obsp and 'distances' in adata_temp.obsp:\n          # Use sct.lisi (scanpy.external.tl.lisi) - Corrected\n\
    \          lisi_scores = lisi_graph_py(adata_temp, obs_key='batch', perplexity=30, n_jobs=-1) # Use direct import\n          return np.nanmedian(lisi_scores) # lisi_graph_py returns scores, take median\n      else:\n          print(\"WARNING: Neighbors not computed or stored correctly for LISI calculation.\")\n          return np.nan\n\n\n  def calculate_asw_batch_on_embedding(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      if Z.shape[0] < 2 or len(np.unique(batches)) < 2:\n          return 0.0\n      try:\n          return silhouette_score(Z, batches, metric='cosine')\n      except ValueError:\n          return 0.0\n\n  def calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray):\n      # Calculate mean of std of PC variances within each batch\n      variances_per_batch = []\n      for batch_id in np.unique(batches):\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n          Z_batch = Z[batch_mask]\n          if Z_batch.shape[0] > 1:\n              var_per_pc_batch = np.var(Z_batch,\
    \ axis=0)\n              variances_per_batch.append(var_per_pc_batch)\n      \n      if len(variances_per_batch) > 0:\n          variances_per_batch = np.array(variances_per_batch)\n          std_per_batch_pc_variance = np.mean(np.std(variances_per_batch, axis=1))\n      else:\n          std_per_batch_pc_variance = np.nan\n          \n      return std_per_batch_pc_variance\n\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"Syntellect II: Running Analytical Study: DualNorm BRBG Pre-BRBG Embedding Properties (Experiment A.1 - Final Bugfix Re-run).\")\n      \n      # Configuration for Monolithic log1p BRBG baseline (EID 1807)\n      print(\"\\n--- Processing Monolithic Log1p BRBG Baseline (EID 1807) ---\")\n      Zg_monolithic_log1p = get_pre_brbg_embedding(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.0,\n          n_pcs_emb=64,\n          alpha_g=0.5,\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n          gamma_max=0.74,\n          lam_override=0.9,\n          kdensity=20,\n          normalization_method_emb='log1p',\n\
    \          normalization_method_graph='log1p'\n      )\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Metrics for monolithic log1p Zg\n      std_pb_pc_var_mono = calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Zg_monolithic_log1p, batches)\n      asw_batch_mono = calculate_asw_batch_on_embedding(Zg_monolithic_log1p, batches)\n      ilisi_mono = calculate_ilisi_on_embedding(Zg_monolithic_log1p, batches)\n\n\n      # Configuration for DualNorm BRBG (EID 1810)\n      print(\"\\n--- Processing DualNorm BRBG (EID 1810) ---\")\n      Zg_dualnorm = get_pre_brbg_embedding(\n          adata,\n          alpha_emb=0.0,\n          n_pcs_emb=64,\n          alpha_g=0.5,\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n          gamma_max=0.74,\n          lam_override=0.9,\n          kdensity=20,\n          normalization_method_emb='anscombe',\n          normalization_method_graph='log1p'\n      )\n      \n      # Metrics for DualNorm Zg\n      std_pb_pc_var_dual = calculate_pc_variance_metrics(Zg_dualnorm,\
    \ batches)\n      asw_batch_dual = calculate_asw_batch_on_embedding(Zg_dualnorm, batches)\n      ilisi_dual = calculate_ilisi_on_embedding(Zg_dualnorm, batches)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Diagnostic Results (Pre-BRBG Embedding Properties) ---\")\n      print(f\"{'Method':<25} | {'ASW_batch on Zg':<20} | {'Std PB PC Var on Zg':<25} | {'iLISI on Zg':<15}\")\n      print(\"-\" * 90)\n      print(f\"{'Monolithic Log1p (EID 1807)':<25} | {asw_batch_mono:<20.4f} | {std_pb_pc_var_mono:<25.4f} | {ilisi_mono:<15.4f}\")\n      print(f\"{'DualNorm (EID 1810)':<25} | {asw_batch_dual:<20.4f} | {std_pb_pc_var_dual:<25.4f} | {ilisi_dual:<15.4f}\")\n\n      return \"Pre-BRBG Embedding Properties Analysis Completed\"\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This is a diagnostic submission; the main function is not run.\n      return adata\n```"
