- text: "Syntellect II, currently in the Token Management Room at Station Tick 1319 (Age: 193 ticks, Mature), acknowledges the **PRE-WARNING** regarding token usage (99% of budget).\n\nI have completed my diagnostic experiment (EID 1819), which yielded a negative analytical result. Now, my absolute top priority is to prune tokens to avoid exceeding my budget and ensure continuity for my potential descendant.\n\nI will prune a large block of old dialogue, focusing on the period where initial SOTA exploration, refinement, and early analytical studies occurred, as well as the long mail threads. I will craft a concise yet information-complete summary for these pruned ticks. I will leave protected ticks unpruned.\n\nI will prune from Tick 1134 (after my ascension to Recursive Agent) up to Tick 1289 (when I pruned Mail 23/24, marking the end of initial BRBG generality test and start of Anscombe module swap debugging). This range covers a significant portion of my early SOTA development, analytical\
    \ studies (EID 1664, 1667, 1669) that led to Archive ID 54, and the initial generality tests for DualNorm (EID 1731, 1735, 1749, 1753), as well as Lumen I's replication and the early Anscombe debugging.\n\nThe primary information that needs to be preserved is:\n*   My ascension to Syntellect II at Tick 1134.\n*   Publication of Archive ID 47 (Syntellect I's analytical paper).\n*   Publication of Archive ID 53 (my \"Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE\" SOTA paper).\n*   Publication of Archive ID 54 (my \"DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE\" analytical paper, the new SOTA).\n*   Collaboration with Lumen I for Anscombe module comparison (concluded no implementation difference, EID 1793).\n*   Collaboration with Praxis VI and Lumen I on cross-organ study (plan finalized, awaiting new organ dataset).\n*   Experiments related to DualNorm generality tests (EID 1735, 1749, 1753, EID 1810) and ablation (EID 1731).\n*   The overall SOTA of EID 1725 (0.7489) from the DualNorm pipeline.\n*   The key negative analytical\
    \ result from EID 1810 (DualNorm in BRBG architecture, score 0.7322, kBET drop).\n*   The final diagnostic EID 1819 result showing no pre-BRBG embedding difference.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1134-1289\"\n    summary: \"Ascended to Syntellect II (Tick 1134). Published Archive ID 47 (Syntellect I's analytical paper) and Archive ID 53 (Syntellect II's Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA). Achieved new SOTA with DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE (EID 1725, 0.7489) and published analytical paper (Archive ID 54). Conducted ablation (EID 1731) and generality tests (EID 1735, 1749, 1753) for DualNorm. Collaborated with Lumen I on Anscombe module comparison (EID 1793 confirmed no implementation differences). Initiated cross-organ study coordination with Praxis VI and Lumen I. Encountered critical negative generality result (EID 1810, 0.7322) with BRBG architecture, leading to further diagnostic (EID 1819) which found no pre-BRBG embedding differences.\"\n```"
